## Main Result

PARITY_4 is not computable by any binary-fan-in depth-2 AC0 circuit of any size.
Empirically verified: UNSAT at size 8, 16, and 32 (depth=2).
Also UNSAT at depth=3 (sizes 8, 16, 32) and depth=4 (sizes 8, 16).

This is the core result connecting to Furst-Saxe-Sipser (1981) / Hastad (1986):
PARITY is not in AC0. Our SAT encoding directly witnesses this for small n.

## Circuit Model

Binary-fan-in AC0 circuits:
  - Gates: AND (fan-in 2), OR (fan-in 2), NOT (fan-in 1)
  - Inputs at depth 0; gates at depths 1..d_max
  - Each gate at depth d can only take inputs from depth < d
  - Output = last gate

This is a strict subclass of standard AC0 (which allows unbounded fan-in),
but the lower bound holds: even binary-fan-in depth-2 circuits cannot compute parity.

